Toronto, November, 23 1993

JANA Publishing is pleased to announce that we have selected
Morse Telecommunications as the exclusive, worldwide distributor of
our current and future Linux products. Effective immediately,
Morse Telecommunications has assumed complete responsibility for
distributing current and future releases of the Linux CD-ROM,
both single copies and subscriptions. Additionally, we are happy to
announce that with this agreement, Morse Telecommunications has agreed
to provide support to our existing Linux customers.

Both of our firms will work together on compiling all future
releases of the Linux CD-ROM. This should result in a better
product for end-users, with Morse Telecommunications providing
technical assistance and recommendations on the Linux compilations,
and JANA Publishing handling the production and quality control.

What does this mean to existing Linux CD-ROM subscribers?

JANA publishing will continue to fullfill existing Linux CD-ROM
subscriptions, but will not accept any further orders for them.
Orders for such subscriptions should be forwarded to order@Morse.Net.
Additionally, existing subscribers can now receive support from Morse
Telecommunications. Refer to the end of this message for contact
information.

What if I want to purchase a Linux CD through JANA?

JANA Publishing no longer sells Linux CD's directly. All orders
are handled by Morse Telecommunications, our exclusive distributor.
With this agreement, you can now get support with your Linux CD-ROM's.

I haven't received my CD yet. Who do I call?

All the Linux CD-ROM's have been mailed out to our existing
customers. Please email linux@jana.com if you haven't
received yours yet. Be sure to include your mailing address.
and we will take care of this ASAP.

What about my subsriptions ?

If you are a subscriber you will continue to get Linux CD-ROM's. The
same CD-ROM that will be sold and suported by Morse Telecommunications.
We will be publishing only 4 CD's a year, but if you have paid for 12 CD's
you will get them. (Eg: Your 2 year subscription has been transfered to a
3 year subscription. ).

