This is a fix for a bug i founf in dosemu0.49
keyboard interrupt handling code.

the bug only manifested itself on my machine when redirecting all
output to /dev/null, so it took some time to find it.

The bug was that the signal handler didnt handle the case when multiple signals
were generated before the previous signals were processed.

fix: (sorry, no diff-file :-(
In file dosipc.c, at function sigipc()
===================
       void sigipc(void)
       {
         struct ipcpkt pkt;
(add)    struct timeval tv;
(add)    fd_set fds;
(add)
(add)    /*signals dont queue, but packets do*/
(add)    do{
             I_printf("IPC .....
====================

====================
             default:
                  I_printf("IPC: (par) .....
             }
(add)        /* if any other packets arrived with the same signal */
(add)        FD_ZERO(&fds);
(add)        FD_SET(PARENT_FD,&fds);
(add)        tv.tv_sec=0;
(add)        tv.tv_usec=0;
(add)     } while( select(255,&fds,NULL,NULL,&tv)==1 );
        }
=====================

with this patch, keyboard interrupts seems to be working excellent for me.
The game Pinball Dreams now works perfectly for me.

Thanks for the truly excellent application dosemu to all that have worked with it.

yours sincerely, ronnie s.

ronnie@lysator.liu.se

