One of my UNIX friends pointed out a symptom of my MS-DOS programmer's
disease:  using '/' to introduce command line options.  TDE v3.2 would not
edit files with '/' as the first character, e.g. tde /test/me.  TDE v3.2a
fixes this quirk in the UNIX operating system ;*).  The '-' character is used
to introduce command line options.

The source (tde3.2a.src.zip) for the Linux port is on SunSite.unc.edu.
A static executable (tde3.2a.zip) is also available at SunSite.unc.edu.

The static Linux executable was builded with:

   Linux .99.pl.12
   SLS 1.03
   gcc 2.4.5
   ncurses 1.8

