Pidentd (stands for Peter's IDENT Daemon, or perhaps it is the 
Portable IDENT Daemon?) is a server that implements the IDENT
protocol as specified by RFC 1413. It is useful to find out the
username of a remote user that initiates a TCP connection. Many
new TCP/IP servers try to use the IDENT protocol, for example
Sendmail 8, the Wuarchive FTPD, many LPMUDs and more. More than
10 million IDENT-protocol packets where transmitted over the NSFnet
backbone last month.

Pidentd version 2 now supports Linux 0.99.13q or later as of Pidentd
version 2.2beta.2. It can be FTP'd from ftp.lysator.liu.se in
pub/ident/servers as pidentd-2.2beta.2.tar.gz, or from ftp.uu.net which
mirrors ftp.lysator.liu.se into the directory networking/ident/servers.

The Linux patches are based on Pauline Middelink's authd (which is a
modified Pidentd version 1 server).

