    tsx-11.mit.edu:/pub/linux/BETA/loop
and nic.funet.fi:/pub/OS/Linux/BETA/loop

The file is:

lo.2.tar.gz	The loop devices patch

The DES encryption module didn't change, so you can still use the old
des.1.tar.gz

Note: If you're FTPing from outside the U.S. or Canada, please get the
      DES patch from nic.funet.fi, because of the well-known US export
      restrictions.

(DES encryption is optional. The loop devices also work without it.)

Loop devices give you the ability to mount file systems from regular
files. Additionally, you can use them to have more than one file system
on one partition and to have transparent on-line encryption of all your
data.

The loop devices patch is relative to ALPHA-0.99pl13s (also works with
a few earlier alpha versions). The DES patch should work with any recent
kernel.

This version is simply an update to the new kernel. There are no
"interesting" changes. I'm releasing it now for an intermediate kernel
version because many people have been asking for it. I hope this patch
will go into the final 0.99pl14 without undue problems.

The DES code is derived from Eric Young's DES library. I will replace
it with a faster DES algorithm when I have time to experiment a bit with
it. (Yes, I know I've already said this more than three months ago ...)

I've attached the CHANGES file section.

